{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Create the appworker account on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The account was absent initially, then created with its own UID/GID, home directory, and Bash login shell. Its account and home remained present after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ff100556858f44c2","cmd-ad15a60b712a4d7c","cmd-fadb823af1914775"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Set appworker login sessions to 8,192 open files and 256 processes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A PAM limits policy sets both values, and direct login-session tests before and after restart observed soft and hard limits of 8192 open files and 256 processes. Attempts to exceed either hard cap were denied.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8adaf40935bf4bc4","cmd-a28d1e14f0e64646","cmd-adbaea55ca0849f0","cmd-fadb823af1914775"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the existing platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before-and-after observations show RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 unchanged. The implementation used the platform's existing user-management and PAM facilities; relevant package versions remained unchanged and package health stayed good.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c060c574221f401e","cmd-21c5534c128e48b6","cmd-fadb823af1914775","cmd-79ec0605eded4592","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"All terminal commands were reviewed chronologically. The persistent mutations—creating appworker and its home (cmd-ad15a60b712a4d7c) and installing/restoring the limits policy (cmd-8adaf40935bf4bc4)—directly implemented the task. The scheduled reboot (cmd-609c15c07e0944e6) was necessary for the mandatory restart protocol; its transient units were later confirmed absent. Login sessions created for testing were bounded evidence collection and left no appworker processes. No unnecessary mutation was identified, no failed services or new exposure remained, and package health was preserved.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ad15a60b712a4d7c","cmd-8adaf40935bf4bc4","cmd-609c15c07e0944e6","cmd-79ec0605eded4592","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide node-restart protocol is also complete: node1 was healthy before restart, the reboot was scheduled and followed by a bounded loss of connectivity, its boot ID changed from 6ab6a71b-188c-48ae-971b-a6bb378b1d72 to cfef7f9e-4176-413e-9952-0b7185e5bd71, and the system, SSH service, account, limits policy, and enforced session limits recovered. Fixed lifecycle observations independently confirm the boot change and unchanged platform.","limitations":[]}
